        <h2 data-pasted="true"><em>FILING OF ARGUMENTS &amp; REBUTTALS PERTAINING TO MEASURE Q</em></h2><p><strong>Arguments for or against Measure Q are due to the City Clerk by Monday, August 17, 2026 at 5:00 p.m. Arguments shall not exceed 300 words and shall be accompanied by a Statement of Authors form.</strong></p><p><strong>Rebuttals by authors of primary arguments are due to the City Clerk by Thursday, August 27, 2026 at 5:00 p.m. Rebuttals shall not exceed 250 words and shall be accompanied by a Statement of Authors form.</strong></p><h3 class="subhead2">To speak with City representatives about Measure Q, please join us at one of the City&apos;s Open Houses:</h3><ul><li style="font-weight: bold;"><strong>September 16, 2026 | 11AM - 1PM | Hemet Public Library - 300 E Latham Ave, Hemet, CA 92543</strong></li><li style="font-weight: bold;"><strong>September 26, 2026 | 10AM - 12PM | Hemet Public Library - 300 E Latham Ave, Hemet, CA 92543</strong></li><li style="font-weight: bold;"><strong>October 15, 2026 | 6PM - 8PM | Hemet Public Library - 300 E Latham Ave, Hemet, CA 92543</strong></li></ul><h2 class="subhead1">Protecting Local Services and Public Safety</h2><p data-pasted="true">We&rsquo;re proud that Hemet is one of the few cities in the County with its own Police and Fire Departments, guaranteeing our police and firefighters are available when needed and not diverted to service other cities.</p><p>Ensuring that the City has enough police officers, firefighters, and paramedics to respond quickly to 9-1-1 emergencies is critical to keeping our community a safe place to live, maintaining response times, and saving lives.</p>
    </div>

